# Definition of Ready

A task is ready when:

- Requirements are understood
- Dependencies identified
- UI references available
- Acceptance criteria defined
- Required documentation completed

---

# Definition of Done

A task is complete only when:

- Code implemented
- Reviewed
- Tested
- Responsive
- Accessible
- Documented
- No TypeScript errors
- No lint errors
- Successfully committed to Git

---

# Git Commit Strategy

Commit after each completed feature.

Examples:

feat(auth): implement secure login

feat(layout): build responsive application shell

feat(dashboard): create dashboard framework

feat(core): configure application infrastructure

refactor: improve project architecture

docs: update sprint documentation

